	<dict>
		<key>NSAllowsArbitraryLoads</key>
		<true/>
		<key>NSAllowsLocalNetworking</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
	<key>NSBonjourServices</key>
	<array>
		<string>_thomascreek._tcp</string>
	</array>
	<key>NSFaceIDUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Face ID confirms it's you before a door, lock, camera or oven changes.</string>
	<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Finds the Thomas Creek hub on your home Wi-Fi.</string>
	<key>NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Lets Thomas Creek notice when you leave or get home, even when the app is closed, so the last one out gets a check of the doors and garage. Your location stays on this iPhone; only "arrived" or "left" is sent home, plus a rough location (about a kilometre) when you ask for the weather where you are.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Thomas Creek notices when you get home or leave, to check the doors and garage, and shows the weather where you are.</string>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Lets you talk to Thomas Creek. Your voice is turned into text on this iPhone.</string>
	<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Turns what you say to Thomas Creek into text, on this iPhone when it can.</string>
	<key>NSSupportsLiveActivities</key>
	<true/>
	<key>NSSupportsLiveActivitiesFrequentUpdates</key>
	<true/>
